  "id": "Compound::DB00808 - Gene::763",
  "verbalization": "Indapamide is likely to interact with Ca5a through a mechanism involving the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, as evidenced by its binding to Ca12 or Ca4, which in turn participate in this biochemical process. The presence of multiple pathways linking Indapamide to Ca5a through the same intermediate (reversible hydration of carbon dioxide) suggests a shared functional role in the metabolic pathway. The consistent involvement of Ca5a in this process, as indicated by its participation in the activity, implies that Indapamide may influence the physiological function of Ca5a through this indirect route. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Indapamide in modulating carbon dioxide metabolism, which could have implications for cellular function and homeostasis.",
